From be1a6b4e7cd62adc8cc8d2e8636289f6cc3d3911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:03:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 50/69] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250-motorola-nairo: Add backlight
 and fuel gauge

- Enable the PM8150L WLED with the downstream settings (four strings,
  20.5 V OVP, 1050 mA boost limit), limited to 20 mA per string because
  early PM8150L revisions cannot do the 25 mA default, and link it to the
  bootloader framebuffer so blanking turns the panel off.
- Enable the PM7250B fuel gauge, and describe the battery's minimum
  voltage (the downstream QG cutoff) and the OCV tables of the Amperex
  cell, converted from the downstream qcom,pc-temp-v2-lut profile.
- Sort the node references.

The OVP and boost values are valid for the WLED5 block per the driver's
tables, but the qcom-wled binding currently only lists the WLED4 values.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
